  "measurement": "Each stage is a fresh Linux process pinned to one logical CPU. Wall time includes I/O. Hashing and comparison are separate. Other jobs used other logical CPUs. One final timed pass per profile. RSS is Linux wait4, includes any pre-exec launcher high-water mark and excludes the filesystem cache. Temporary bytes are the largest sampled sum of unlinked regular-file sizes in the child process, sampled every 50 ms; destination is separate.",
